 "function": "cloudgen.climate.hadley_edge_raw_deg",
 "doc": "Held-Hou raw Hadley edge (degrees, NOT clamped, inf for no spin) of a seeded table of 400 random bodies (period of either sign, radius, gravity, scale height log-uniform), which crosses every clamp and the eddy threshold. Float64 closed form (sqrt, a few products): rtol 1e-9, a 1-ulp nudge of every input of the regular rows moves the result by under 2e-15 relative (a nudge of a degenerate row can cross its branch). inf is compared as inf. Python details a port must copy: gravity * scale height goes through max(0.0, g H), which returns 0.0 for a NaN product (Rust f64::max ignores a NaN operand too; clamp does not); a non-finite or zero period (None, NaN, +-inf, +-0) gives inf; a NaN radius gives NaN. NaN and infinities may appear in the inputs (a rotation period None is stored as NaN) and in the outputs: NaN equals NaN, an infinity equals the same infinity (sign included).",
